WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.082
Deep learning depends on huge datasets that are
costly to store, preprocess,

00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:08.243
and train on.

00:00:08.323 --> 00:00:12.405
Dataset distillation compresses a dataset into a
tiny synthetic one that still trains high-accuracy models.

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:16.566
This paper introduces SPEED,

00:00:16.646 --> 00:00:20.728
Sparse Parameterization for Epitomic dataset Distillation.

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:24.889
Instead of tuning the matching objective like most
prior work,

00:00:24.969 --> 00:00:29.051
SPEED rethinks how the synthetic dataset itself is
parameterized.

00:00:29.131 --> 00:00:33.212
It borrows ideas from dictionary learning and
sparse coding: a shared pool of spatial-agnostic

00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:37.374
epitomic tokens acts as a dictionary,

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:41.535
sparse coding matrices pick the significant tokens
per image,

00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:45.697
and a feature-recurrent network reassembles them
into high-resolution synthetic images.

00:00:45.777 --> 00:00:49.858
The result is state-of-the-art distillation,

00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:54.020
especially on high-resolution ImageNet subsets,
with a fraction of the storage.
